    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
 
    <section id="about">
      <h2>About</h2>
      <p>
        Friends of Palo Alto Library are proud to present a monthly book sale of over 50,000 wonderful used books, records, videos, magazines, and more.
        Support the library by purchasing our low-priced books from the nicest booksellers around.
        <strong>100% of proceeds go to the Palo Alto Library.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        The sale takes place at the Cubberly Community Center one Saturday a month.
        Check our <a href="#">Sale Calendar</a> for the next sale!
      </p>
      <p>
        The Friends of Palo Alto Library are always accepting book and media donations in our main room.
      </p>
    </section>

   
    <section id="sale-rooms">
      <h2>Sale Rooms</h2>
      <p><strong>Main Sale Room:</strong> The main sale room has paperback and hardbound books as well as gift cards.</p>
      <p><strong>New Room:</strong> Children’s books, music, DVDs, toys, and foreign language books.</p>
      <p><strong>K6 & K7:</strong> Sunday bargain rooms. Books are 50% off in these rooms on Sunday. We also offer a $5 fill-a-bag deal on Sunday — purchase a shopping bag from us and fill it up!</p>
      <img src="book-sale.jpg" alt="Friends of Palo Alto Library Book Sale">
    </section>

    <section id="calendar">
      <h2>Sale Hours & Calendar</h2>
      <p>Sales happen on the first Saturday of the month.</p>
      <p>Our next sale is on <strong>November 1, 2025</strong>.</p>

      <div class="sale-hours">
        <h3>Saturday</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Tickets</td><td>8 AM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bargain Room</td><td>11 AM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Main Room</td><td>11 AM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>New Room</td><td>11 AM</td></tr>
        </table>

        <h3>Sunday</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Bargain Room</td><td>10 AM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Main Room</td><td>11 AM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>New Room</td><td>11 AM</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

 
    <section id="location">
      <h2>Location</h2>
      <iframe src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d6337.663007426973!2d-122.11280642424651!3d37.417457332662785!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x808fba6d6967fff5%3A0x1fe0687789f22d6b!2sFriends%20of%20the%20Palo%20Alto%20Library!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sus!4v1761076576528!5m2!1sen!2sus"
        allowfullscreen=""
        loading="lazy"
        referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
    </section>

 
    <section id="policies">
      <h2>Sale Policies</h2>
      <h3>Line Policy</h3>
      <p>
        The sales line operates on a numbered ticket system. Shoppers may begin to line up at 8 AM to receive their tickets, which hold their spot in line, enabling them to leave the sale and return when the doors open.
        There is a two-ticket-per-person limit.
      </p>

      <h3>Twelve Book Policy</h3>
      <p>
        We have a sale policy of no more than twelve books per shopper before noon, due to the high number of shoppers.
        The limitation continues after noon if there is still a line outside. Once there is no longer a line, shoppers may purchase more than twelve books.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2025 Friends of Palo Alto Library | All proceeds support the Palo Alto Library</p>
  </footer>
